# Routines whose bodies are hand-written rather than generated. apple2tc emits
# a declaration for each and rewrites every call site to it; the definitions
# live in a2rom.c and game.c, stitched into one translation unit by
# snake-byte-ext.c.
#
# The file is still called rom.externs for history's sake -- it began as ROM
# entry points only. It now also carries game routines, which is the point of
# the exercise: every line moved from the second list to a readable definition
# is a piece of Snake Byte that no longer looks like a decompiler's output.
#
# apple2tc takes a single --extern-routines= path, so both lists share a file.

# Apple II ROM entry points -- a2rom.c
F800 rom_plot
F819 rom_hline
F864 rom_setcol
F871 rom_scrn
FC58 rom_home
FC68 rom_fc68
FDED rom_cout
FE89 rom_setkbd
FE93 rom_setvid

# Snake Byte's own routines -- game.c
6127 game_load_shape
60E7 game_draw_cell
60E4 game_plot_shape
6148 game_plot_hline
615A game_plot_vline
6256 game_start_round
6288 game_play_loop
72CE game_draw_status
78B3 game_bonus
7980 game_setup
7019 game_next_byte
7024 game_set_ink
7000 game_lores_vline
71F3 game_print_bcd
7226 game_print_zero_if_blank
7267 game_add_score
702B game_clear_hgr
# $6C4B (game_rand_byte) was here and is deliberately gone. Its adapter was dead
# -- every caller is hand-written C reaching game_rand_byte_native() directly --
# and the mapping went with it, because nothing generated calls $6C4B either, so
# it is unreachable and pruned whether or not it is externalised. Measured: the
# only effect of the line was the declaration it emitted, 37 bytes.
#
# Worth knowing before adding an entry: a mapping for a routine no generated
# code calls buys nothing. This is not how a routine gets deleted.
6B93 game_plot_shape_merge
7045 game_draw_playfield
6641 game_install_cout_hook
660F game_start_life_adapter
6BEF game_mark_head
